            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://www.ciclista.de/media/posts/28/20240602_0178.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <blockquote>
<p>from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Italian_language" title="Italian language">Italian</a> <i><i lang="ang"><a href="https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tenebroso#Old_English" class="extiw" title="wikt:tenebroso">tenebroso</a></i></i> ("dark, gloomy, mysterious"), also occasionally called dramatic illumination, is a style of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Painting" title="Painting">painting</a> using especially pronounced <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiaroscuro" title="Chiaroscuro">chiaroscuro</a>, where there are violent contrasts of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light" title="Light">light</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness" title="Darkness">dark</a>, and where darkness becomes a dominating feature of the image. The technique was developed to add drama to an image through a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spotlight_(theatre_lighting)" title="Spotlight (theatre lighting)">spotlight</a> effect. [from wikipedia]</p>
</blockquote>
